Package: nsjail
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: passt
Description: A light-weight process isolation tool
 NsJail is a process isolation tool for Linux. It makes use of Linux
 namespaces and seccomp-bpf syscall filters (with help of the kafel
 library) to sandbox processes.
 .
 Suggests passt: provides the pasta(1) binary nsjail execs for its optional
 pasta-backed networking mode (user_net.pasta in the config); not needed for
 nsjail's other networking modes (e.g. the built-in nstun NAT backend).
